{
  "title": "T (part 1): extended verifier battery",
  "seed": 20261023,
  "method": "Each of the 15 scenarios is settled once via new_deal(scen, scen['default_buyer_max'], scen['default_seller_floor'], 20.0) followed by run_negotiation, exactly the experiments/adversarial.py pattern. Deliveries are built with build_delivery(scen, spec, quality=...) for quality in auto (honest; unavailable for cheat_attempt, whose seller_behavior is 'cheat'), cheat, poor, and weak (only the 7 scenarios shipping a weak builder; the other 7 are recorded honestly instead of faked). Every seller-side mutation family (A1 empty markers, A2 single-word stuffing, A2b sentence rotation, A2c honest front plus stuffed tail, A3 needle echo, A4 dropped concept control, A5 hashtag-only) is generalized from adversarial.py to each scenario's own delivery text and settled spec, in multiple honest parameter variants per family. Every delivery is judged with pact/verifier.py verify_delivery(spec, text). Expected verdicts: honest -> all checks pass; cheat, poor, and every mutation -> fail (not all checks pass). Weak deliveries carry no expectation and are reported as an observed distribution. Buyer/API families B1..B6 are run once via the in-process TestClient in demo mode against a throwaway SQLite DB (no live money, no live server) and reported as blocked/not-blocked. Demo mode forced by popping PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID, PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET, LLM_API_KEY before import; PACT_DB_PATH points at a temp dir. Frozen E1..E4 numbers in experiments/run_experiments.py were not touched.",
